{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '4850,4885p'; rg -n \\\"PlanDigest|bundle\\\\.Payload\\\\.Plan\\\\.PlanDigest|plan_digest\\\" pose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '1,100p'\"","aggregated_output":"---\ntype: decision-log\nslug: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\nowner: @pose-maintainers\nsensitivity: public-internal\ncreated_at: 2026-08-13\nlast_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\nexpires_at: 2026-11-11\nsource_refs:\n  spec: \"pose-component-aware-review-plans\"\n  workflow: \"feature\"\n  commands: [\"pose assess discover --component pose-mcp/internal/pose\", \"pose lint-spec pose-component-aware-review-plans --ready-check\"]\n  external_sources: []  # [{url: \"\", accessed_at: \"YYYY-MM-DD\"}]\n---\n\n# decision-log: adr-component-aware-review-plans-review\n\n## Context\n\nPOSE 1.0 binds immutable review attempts to a scope-kind profile but does not\ncompose criteria or tool guidance from the mapped components. The implementation\nintroduces a public schema-v2 policy/profile contract, CLI/MCP projections and a\nnew plan digest, so the design needs an explicit future-review trigger.\n\n## Current state\n\nADR `2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans` is accepted. It chooses\ntyped one-level overlays, deterministic union into one effective plan, a closed\nnative-tool catalog and additive schema-v1 compatibility. Implementation is\ntracked by `pose-component-aware-review-plans`.\n\n## Next checks\n\n- Verify frontend, backend and multi-component golden plans.\n- Verify command/path/symlink/selector negative cases.\n- Verify CLI/MCP schema parity and scaffold distribution.\n- Review production false-staleness before 2026-11-11.\n\n## Risks\n\nComponent maps can be stale and overlay composition can make unrelated metadata\ninvalidate approvals. Keep mapping provenance visible, include only consumed\ninputs in the digest and reject conflicts instead of selecting heuristically.\n\n## Next owner\n\n`@pose-maintainers`.\n\n## References\n\n- `spec:pose-component-aware-review-plans`\n- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n- https://github.com/oseiaspereira88/pose/issues/13 (accessed 2026-08-13)\n  4850\t\t\treturn false\n  4851\t\t}\n  4852\t\tfor _, blocker := range currentBlockers {\n  4853\t\t\tif blocker == now.Ref || strings.HasPrefix(blocker, now.Ref+\":\") {\n  4854\t\t\t\treturn false\n  4855\t\t\t}\n  4856\t\t}\n  4857\t\treturn true\n  4858\t}\n  4859\t\n  4860\t// sameRoadmapApartFromLifecycle reports whether a roadmap's committed file holds\n  4861\t// the same between two revisions, but for its transition to done.\n  4862\tfunc (s Store) sameRoadmapApartFromLifecycle(identity ArtifactRef, from, to string) bool {\n  4863\t\tif identity.Kind != \"roadmap\" && identity.Kind != \"milestone\" {\n  4864\t\t\treturn false\n  4865\t\t}\n  4866\t\trm, err := s.GetRoadmap(identity.Slug)\n  4867\t\tif err != nil {\n  4868\t\t\treturn false\n  4869\t\t}\n  4870\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(s.Root, rm.Path)\n  4871\t\tif err != nil {\n  4872\t\t\treturn false\n  4873\t\t}\n  4874\t\trel = filepath.ToSlash(rel)\n  4875\t\tfiles := s.fsys()\n  4876\t\tproducer := governanceProducerFromFiles(files, \"review\")\n  4877\t\tthen, err := captureGovernanceGit(files, s.Root, producer, \"show\", from+\":\"+rel)\n  4878\t\tif err != nil {\n  4879\t\t\tif hasGitMetadataIn(files, s.Root) {\n  4880\t\t\t\tmarkGovernanceReadUnknownForProject(files, s.Root, \"\", producer, \"the earlier roadmap revision could not be read from Git\")\n  4881\t\t\t}\n  4882\t\t\treturn false\n  4883\t\t}\n  4884\t\tnow, err := captureGovernanceGit(files, s.Root, producer, \"show\", to+\":\"+rel)\n  4885\t\tif err != nil {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:127:\tPlanDigest     string                `json:\"plan_digest\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:519:\tbundlePlanDigest, err := reviewBundlePlanDigest(plan)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:523:\tbundle.Payload.Plan = ReviewBundlePlan{DelegatedRunProofRequired: plan.DelegatedRunProofRequired, Limitations: append([]string(nil), plan.Limitations...), PlanDigest: bundlePlanDigest, Independence: plan.Independence, Components: append([]ReviewPlanComponent{}, plan.Components...), Criteria: append([]ReviewPlanCriterion{}, plan.Criteria...), Tools: append([]ReviewPlanTool{}, plan.Tools...), SelectedProfiles: append([]ReviewPlanProfile{}, plan.SelectedProfiles...), Structure: plan.Structure, CloseoutReview: plan.CloseoutReview, AcceptedLimits: append([]ReviewAcceptedLimit(nil), plan.AcceptedLimits...)}\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1933:\tplanDigest, _ := reviewBundlePlanDigest(plan)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1965:func reviewBundlePlanDigest(plan ReviewPlan) (string, error) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4846:\tif then.PlanDigest == \"\" || then.PlanDigest != now.PlanDigest || !slices.Equal(then.GoverningContracts, now.GoverningContracts) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:60:\tPlanDigest           string                        `json:\"plan_digest,omitempty\"`\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:520:\t\t\t\tentry.ImplementationDigest, entry.PlanDigest = subjectDigest, planDigest\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:708:\tBundleID, BundleDigest, SubjectDigest, PlanDigest string\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:733:\treturn result.BundleID, result.BundleDigest, result.SubjectDigest, result.PlanDigest, result.Contracts, result.Evidence, result.Blockers\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:774:\t\t\treturn bundle.BundleID, bundle.BundleDigest, bundle.Payload.Subject.ImplementationDigest, bundle.Payload.Plan.PlanDigest, bundle.Payload.GoverningContracts, nil, []string{scope + \":source-delivery-target-missing\"}\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:778:\t\t\treturn bundle.BundleID, bundle.BundleDigest, bundle.Payload.Subject.ImplementationDigest, bundle.Payload.Plan.PlanDigest, bundle.Payload.GoverningContracts, nil, []string{scope + \":source-delivery-profile-unavailable\"}\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:809:\t\treturn bundle.BundleID, bundle.BundleDigest, bundle.Payload.Subject.ImplementationDigest, bundle.Payload.Plan.PlanDigest, bundle.Payload.GoverningContracts, proof, uniqueSorted(blockers)\npose-mcp/internal/pose/federated_acceptance.go:811:\treturn bundle.BundleID, bundle.BundleDigest, bundle.Payload.Subject.ImplementationDigest, bundle.Payload.Plan.PlanDigest, bundle.Payload.GoverningContracts, federatedBundleEvidence(files, bundle, eligible), nil\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
