{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '1990,2010p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1990\t\n  1991\tfunc reviewBundlePayloadDigest(payload ReviewBundlePayload) (string, error) {\n  1992\t\tcanonical := payload\n  1993\t\t// Change-set IDs and Git refs remain exported for audit/debugging but are\n  1994\t\t// advisory provenance. Stable subject identity is the classified patch and\n  1995\t\t// tree manifest, so provider ref movement or a derived-only follow-up commit\n  1996\t\t// cannot change the bundle identity.\n  1997\t\tcanonical.Subject.ChangeSets = nil\n  1998\t\tcanonical.Subject.Base = \"\"\n  1999\t\tcanonical.Subject.Head = \"\"\n  2000\t\t// The observation is derived from the head just cleared above, so sealing\n  2001\t\t// it would smuggle that ref back into the identity: a provider ref moving,\n  2002\t\t// or a derived-only follow-up commit, would flip a result from observed to\n  2003\t\t// carried-forward and stale a review of content that did not move. It stays\n  2004\t\t// in the written bundle for the reader, as advisory provenance, exactly\n  2005\t\t// like the refs it is computed from.\n  2006\t\t//\n  2007\t\t// Copied first: `canonical := payload` shares the slice backing array, so\n  2008\t\t// clearing in place would erase the state on the bundle the caller is\n  2009\t\t// holding, not on the copy being hashed.\n  2010\t\tcanonical.Evidence = append([]ReviewBundleEvidence{}, canonical.Evidence...)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n### Finding\n\n- **Medium, blocker** — [review_bundle.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-2783063900/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1977) copies `accepted_limits` into the sealed plan, but omits it from the bundle’s `plan_digest` input. Different limits can therefore share the same plan digest, contrary to R1/D2. The outer bundle digest includes the limits, but does not satisfy the separate plan-digest requirement.\n\nThe focused Go tests passed. Both strict validation commands were blocked because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating temporary build directories and accessing its cache; the sealed evidence records passing build, e2e, integration, and unit checks for `pose-mcp`. The review applied the review workflow and the backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules. The recurrence check flagged no clusters.\n\nPOSE accepted the draft check for the conclusion below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go\",\n      \"line\": 1977,\n      \"summary\": \"The bundle copies AcceptedLimits into its sealed plan, but reviewBundlePlanDigest omits the field from the digest input. Different accepted limits therefore produce the same bundle plan_digest and review-plan consumed-input digest, contrary to R1/D2. Include accepted_limits with omitempty in that digest and cover both populated and empty cases.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N1\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:4085; focused AcceptedLimit Go tests passed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N2\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1191-1209; focused ReadyCheckJudges Go test passed\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the accepted-limit parser and reason validation, plan and bundle serialization/digest paths, brief/11 rendering and digest fixture, draft-to-attestation conversion, within-limit preflight, lint-spec ready-check and ADR I/O handling, English/Portuguese manual and scaffold copies, and all listed changed source paths. Checked L1 and L2 against D1/D2; semantic applicability remains a reviewer judgment as the brief says. No other in-scope defect established.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-d8353053d400dc6b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified L1 and L2, their cited reasons, the sealing path, and the brief instructions. L1 explicitly leaves breadth to reviewer judgment and instructs reviewers to dispute overbroad limits; L2's edit-after-seal risk is covered by the full bundle digest. The narrower bundle plan_digest omission is reported as N1. Whether a finding semantically falls inside a limit remains an unresolved reviewer judgment, not an engine-verifiable fact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The change adds local parsing and review-record fields, no shared mutable state or background lifecycle. Focused Go tests passed; the existing bundle publication integration remains sealed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Optional fields preserve prior record meaning, but the bundle plan_digest omits the new review input.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Malformed entries are reported; unsealed limit IDs and whitespace-only within-limit reasons are refused; ADR directory and file read failures fail closed. Focused AcceptedLimit and ReadyCheckJudges tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new field flows through the existing plan, bundle, brief, and conclusion path; no external provider contract changed. The integration assessment's three unobserved HTTP endpoints are unrelated to this change.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Preflight and lint failures identify the unsealed ID, missing reason, or unreadable ADR path; the added paths do not log limit contents or sensitive data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"New JSON fields are optional and omitted when empty; the brief uses version 11, leaving earlier templates and their digests intact. The populated plan-digest omission is tracked separately as N1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The ordinary plan digest includes limits, but the bundle's own effective plan digest does not, so the declared D2 binding is incomplete.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-d8353053d400dc6b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1's explicit within-limit disposition addresses repeated review churn by allowing classification against a declared boundary while keeping disputes blocking. D2 correctly chooses sealing; N1 identifies the missing field in the bundle plan digest implementation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected the English and Brazilian Portuguese manuals, scaffold copies, and version-11 brief text; they describe the runtime sealed-ID and reason checks consistently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Failure messages say which declared ID was not sealed, when a reason is absent, and which ADR could not be read, giving the operator a clear correction.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N1\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R1/D2 require limits to enter the plan digest; ReviewPlan.PlanDigest does, but ReviewBundlePlan.PlanDigest does not.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-d8353053d400dc6b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The inspected changes implement R1-R4 and D1-D2 in the declared pose-mcp review flow and its manual/scaffold copies; the finding is within that scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Limit text is treated as data, flattened and backticks neutralized for the brief. A within-limit result requires a sealed ID and nonblank rationale, and cannot elevate an unsealed ID. Semantic applicability remains an explicit reviewer decision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-d8353053d400dc6b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A brief-only statement would not bind conclusion records; adding one typed limit field and a preflight check is the smallest sufficient mechanism. The design avoids round caps and broader policy machinery. The plan digest must include this consumed input; N1 is that implementation gap.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required command exited 0. Its output included orphan warnings for the larger current attribution range; I did not treat unrelated paths as defects in this subject.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-d8353053d400dc6b\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the sealed subject with no design deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran without persistence; it discovered the pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment ran and reported three unobserved existing HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp); none is introduced by this change. The subject integration path is covered by the cited sealed evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The scan was incomplete because two unrelated specs have unknown scope; no TODO, FIXME, stub, or panic marker was found in the inspected subject paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only check; the task prohibits recording an attestation, its prerequisite. The attempted command reported no current represented bundle and an unfinished lifecycle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-declared-threat-model\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only check; the task prohibits recording an attestation, its prerequisite. The attempted command reported no current represented bundle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command: \\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Selected backend-go, security, and documentation-style rules, which were applied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"reachability:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-reachability\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required command exited 0 with one target, 236 results, and no findings; the sealed reachability evidence covers the scope.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required command, but the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating temporary build directories and accessing its cache. The sealed build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence covers the changed pose-mcp component.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The required module command hit the same read-only Go workspace/cache limitation. Sealed pose-mcp build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence is passing; the focused AcceptedLimit/Brief/Conclude Go tests also passed locally.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
